{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310847,"nonce":"/FaNZORI+XAdx/9zB7ad1Txp6HI=","title":"hir_to_mir.rs (42,750 lines, 312 methods) is now compiler/src/ir/mir/ — 81 files, none over 2k. Call lowering is a probe chain; probes ...","message":"`compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs` (42,750 lines) is `compiler/src/ir/mir/`, 81\nfiles, largest 1,973. `ir/mod.rs` keeps `pub use mir as hir_to_mir;` so callers\ndid not change. Grouped by role, not by where code used to sit:\n\n    decl/     what must exist before a body is lowered (signatures, metadata,\n              vtables, module __init__, and lower_module itself)\n    stmt/     statements, loops, for_in, switch\n    expr/     dispatch, literals, operators, functions, lambda, exceptions,\n              derives, reflect, variables, casts, construction\n    expr/call/  one module per CALL KIND — see below\n    field/    reads (access) and assignment targets (lvalue)\n    resolve/  HIR names and symbols to MIR ids\n    helpers/  boxing, drops, alloc, type_ids, interfaces, patterns, stdlib, ...\n\n`lower_expression_inner` was 13,469 lines; it is now a ~100-line match, one\nmethod per `HirExprKind`. The `Call` arm alone was 9,578 lines and became\n`expr/call/`: method, resolved_method, stdlib_runtime, stdlib_instance,\nstdlib_static, static_receiver, direct, interface, extern_class, intrinsic,\nenum_ctor, derived, array, future, shader, native_struct, super_call,\nvirtual_dispatch, forward_ref, indirect.\n\n\nCall lowering is a chain of shape probes, and probes FALL THROUGH — every one\nof them, verified by a recursive divergence check, not by eyeballing tails.\n\nA probe cannot signal \"not my shape\" by returning `None`, because `?` inside it\nalready returns `None` to mean \"lowering failed\". Conflating them lets a later\nprobe claim a call that a failed earlier probe had already recognised — a\nsilent dispatch fallthrough, the exact thing\n[[feedback_no_silent_dispatch_fallthrough]] forbids.\n\nSo probes take `fell_through: \u0026mut bool`, set it only when control reaches the\nend, and the `probe!` macro in `expr/call/mod.rs` is the single place that\ncontract lives. `?` keeps meaning abort. This also made extraction verbatim: no\n`return` or `?` inside 10k lines had to be rewritten.\n\n\n- Re-destructure inside the new method (`let HirExprKind::Call { .. } =\n  \u0026expr.kind else { unreachable!() }`) instead of taking bindings as\n  parameters. Bodies move byte-identical and no binding changes type.\n- The guard needs `callee` even when the body does not — always include it.\n- Pass preamble locals by value (`result_type: IrType`, cloned at the call\n  site). Check for reassignment first; format-string hits like\n  `\"result_type={:?}\"` look like assignments to a naive regex.\n- `macro_rules!` must be defined ABOVE the `mod` declarations to be in scope\n  for child modules.\n- A `\u0026self`-derived value (`stdlib_info` holds `\u0026RuntimeFunctionCall`) cannot\n  stay live across a `\u0026mut self` probe call. Clone it at its definition and\n  re-borrow inside the probe: `let x = x.as_ref().map(|(a,b,c)| (*a,*b,c));`\n  keeps the body unchanged.\n\n\n- **Brace counting for block extents is wrong** — `format!(\"{}\")` balances, but\n  any unbalanced brace in a string skews it. Strip strings and line comments\n  first (`/tmp/mirblk.py`), or cut at the next `fn` at the same indent.\n- **A whole method vanished.** The regroup dropped `lower_module` silently and\n  the build error read as a missing method on the struct, with a cascade of\n  bogus deref errors after it because `module`'s type became unknown. Diff the\n  FULL function-name set (old file vs new tree) after any mechanical split —\n  312 vs 311 found it instantly.\n- **`helpers/diagnostics.rs` shadowed the `diagnostics` crate** it called.\n  Renamed to `errors.rs`.\n- **A test \"crash\" that was my own contamination**: `DebugChecksum` TIMEOUTed\n  in the suite (30s harness limit) right after a `cargo build`; standalone it\n  runs in 3.2s cold. Re-ran clean and it passed. Per\n  [[feedback_benchmark_process_hygiene]] — check your own history first.\n\n\n`./run_haxe_tests.sh` → 180 total, **179 pass / 1 fail / 0 crash**. The single\nfailure is pre-existing: `test_generic_ctor_untyped_selfref`, see\n[[bugs_generic_scalar_field_stores_box_pointer]]. Plus\n`cargo run --release -p compiler --example test_rayzor_stdlib_e2e` → 15/15.\n\nCommits: `befb9996` (split), `631f8116` (regroup + names), `c5f33fb6`\n(per-kind arms), `463aa878` (dispatch kinds), `65c50319` (nothing over 2k).\nDesign note: `docs/design/mir_lowering_modularization.md`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_mir_lowering_modularization` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}